<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Amenemhat II</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">20th–19th century BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century-bce">19th century BCE</a> · Also known as Amenemhet II</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Amenemhat II was the third king of the Twelfth Dynasty of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egypt">Egypt</a>, reigning for more than thirty years around the turn of the twentieth and nineteenth centuries BCE. His reign was largely peaceful and prosperous, with expeditions to Sinai and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/land-of-punt">Punt</a> and contacts with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/levant">Levant</a> recorded in an annals inscription from Memphis. He was buried in a pyramid at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dahshur">Dahshur</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/amenemhat-ii.jpg" alt="Amenemhat II" width="320" height="513" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Juan R. Lazaro · CC BY 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Amenemhat_II.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
